nchat-ui patch: media retry for WhatsApp attachments the media servers no longer serve.

Media received through WhatsApp's history sync (everything from before the device was
linked) usually returns HTTP 404/410 from the media servers. WhatsApp Web then asks the
phone to re-upload it ("media retry"); nchat didn't, so those attachments could never be
downloaded. This adds that, using whatsmeow's SendMediaRetryReceipt / events.MediaRetry:

- wmchat.cpp: look up the message's sender and direction (needed for the request) and
  pass them to the Go side.
- gowm.go: remember the download error; on 404/410 request a re-upload and report the
  attachment as "downloading"; route events.MediaRetry to the handler.
- mediaretry.go (new): request bookkeeping, 60 s timeout, decrypt the answer, download
  from the new direct path, store the new path in the file id, notify the result.

Applied automatically by nchat-ui's build.rs; candidate for an upstream PR to nchat.
